ontosec:NFC a owl:Class;
            rdfs:comment "A short-range point-to-point wireless communication technology. The technology is a simple extension of the ISO/IEC 14443 proximity-card standard (contactless card, RFID) that combines the interface of a smartcard and a reader into a single device. An NFC device can communicate with both existing ISO/IEC 14443 smartcards and readers, as well as with other NFC devices, and is thereby compatible with existing contactless infrastructure already in use for public transportation and payment.";
            rdfs:subClassOf ontosec:PANetwork.
ontosec:NFCEnabled a owl:Class;
                   rdfs:comment "The device may be or not equiped with Near Field Communication Ship (NFC).";
